nk\nThanks a lot","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567693166,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODM4NDk1NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3632#issuecomment-528384954"},"message":"\u003e  And yes, the content bulk is tracked by git-annex, that is right\n\nI think something is off here.  Even if most the heavy content is now tracked by git-annex, were they included as regular git objects at some point?  If I'm reading the output correctly, it looks like the connection is getting closed at a 2 GiB limit and that Git sees your objects as around 30 GiB.\n\n* What does `git count-objects -vH` report for the repository?\n\n  This should not be in the GiB range.\n\n* What is the `local annex size` line when you run `git annex info` in the repository?\n\n  This should be where the bulk of the size is reported.  This content isn't pushed to GitHub, so it won't cause you to hit into any of their size limits.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567693166,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI3MzkzMTQ3NA=="},"target":"db710ebdbc924722fd7b6e5cd2aa66fc2f73cc67b3a6e47cccd31093a6890ed8","message":"\u003e  And yes, the content bulk is tracked by git-annex, that is right\n\nI think something is off here.  Even if most of the heavy content is now tracked by git-annex, were some large files included as regular git objects at some point?  If I'm reading the output correctly, it looks like the connection is getting closed at a 2 GiB limit and that Git sees your objects as around 30 GiB.\n\n* What does `git count-objects -vH` report for the repository?\n\n  This should not be in the GiB range.\n\n* What is the `local annex size` line when you run `git annex info` in the repository?\n\n  This should be where the bulk of the size is reported.  This content isn't pushed to GitHub, so it won't cause you to hit into any of their size limits.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"5f28eb6cf9dc13eefe95e9c4af8c2adace24728a"},"timestamp":1567708304,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODUxNTI0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3632#issuecomment-528515242"},"message":"Hi @kyleam,\n\nThanks for your help, really appreciate it\n\nI run:\n```\n$ git count-objects -vH\n```\nAnd got the following output:\n```\ncount: 209\nsize: 818.31 MiB\nin-pack: 33\npacks: 1\nsize-pack: 30.47 GiB\nprune-packable: 0\ngarbage: 0\nsize-garbage: 0 bytes\n```\nThen\n```\ngit annex info\n```\n```\nrepository mode: indirect\ntrusted repositories: 0\nsemitrusted repositories: 3\n\t00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 -- web\n \t00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002 -- bittorrent\n \t887fe4cf-571b-4503-94f1-c453416e0c67 -- giuly@giuly-ThinkPad-T480s:~/Documents/NeuroHub/conp-dataset/projects/FRDR-multimodal-dataset [here]\nuntrusted repositories: 0\ntransfers in progress: none\navailable local disk space: 832.87 gigabytes (+1 megabyte reserved)\nlocal annex keys: 0\nlocal annex size: 0 bytes\nannexed files in working tree: 0\nsize of annexed files in working tree: 0 bytes\nbloom filter size: 32 mebibytes (0% full)\nbackend usage: \n```","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"5f28eb6cf9dc13eefe95e9c4af8c2adace24728a"},"timestamp":1567708304,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI3NDA2NjM0NQ=="},"target":"adeb96efdeea1118f1d58b903942e4d13aca7b3f1cc87dc749f5935fd61e30f8","message":"Hi @kyleam,\n\nThanks for your help, really appreciate it\n\nI run:\n```\n$ git count-objects -vH\n```\nAnd got the following output:\n```\ncount: 209\nsize: 818.31 MiB\nin-pack: 33\npacks: 1\nsize-pack: 30.47 GiB\nprune-packable: 0\ngarbage: 0\nsize-garbage: 0 bytes\n```\nThen\n```\ngit annex info\n```\n```\nrepository mode: indirect\ntrusted repositories: 0\nsemitrusted repositories: 3\n\t00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 -- web\n \t00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002 -- bittorrent\n \t887fe4cf-571b-4503-94f1-c453416e0c67 -- id@host:~/Documents/path/projects/dataset [here]\nuntrusted repositories: 0\ntransfers in progress: none\navailable local disk space: 832.87 gigabytes (+1 megabyte reserved)\nlocal annex keys: 0\nlocal annex size: 0 bytes\nannexed files in working tree: 0\nsize of annexed files in working tree: 0 bytes\nbloom filter size: 32 mebibytes (0% full)\nbackend usage: \n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567710309,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODUyODg5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3632#issuecomment-528528893"},"message":"Thanks for reporting back.\n\n\u003e ```\n\u003e $ git count-objects -vH\n\u003e [...]\n\u003e size-pack: 30.47 GiB\n\u003e ```\n\nThis is why GitHub is rejecting your push.  Your repo has ~30 GiB stored as regular git objects.  You have no files tracked by git-annex:\n\n\u003e ```\n\u003e git annex info\n\u003e [...]\n\u003e local annex keys: 0\n\u003e local annex size: 0 bytes\n\u003e annexed files in working tree: 0\n\u003e size of annexed files in working tree: 0 bytes\n\u003e ```\n\nThe only solution to make this work with GitHub is removing those large git objects from the repo (throughout the entire history of the branch you're trying to push) and then track those large files with git-annex instead.  You could rewrite the history to do this, but unless there's important information in the history, it'd be easiest to back up the current repo (just in case), wipe out the .git/ directory, and start fresh.  Make sure those large files get added to the annex, not git.\n\n---\n\nIn terms of the original error reported, I don't think there's much to be done on DataLad's end, so I'll close this issue, but feel free to follow up with questions.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567710310,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjYxMTkwMzI0OQ=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"5f28eb6cf9dc13eefe95e9c4af8c2adace24728a"},"timestamp":1567716778,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODU3NzE1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3632#issuecomment-528577153"},"message":"Hi,\n\nThanks a lot for your help,\n\nI had the suspect it was something like this when I saw annex size 0 bytes\nbut I wonder, I thought github would accept ~50GiB and I was sure that\ndatalad commands would trigger git-annex automatically to add those files.\n\nMaybe this can be implemented if the file content is higher than a certain\nthreshold.\n\nBest\nGiulia\n\n\n\nIl giorno gio 5 set 2019 alle ore 15:05 Kyle Meyer \u003cnotifications@github.com\u003e\nha scritto:\n\n\u003e Thanks for reporting back.\n\u003e\n\u003e $ git count-objects -vH\n\u003e [...]\n\u003e size-pack: 30.47 GiB\n\u003e\n\u003e This is why GitHub is rejecting your push. Your repo has ~30 GiB stored as\n\u003e regular git objects. You have no files tracked by git-annex:\n\u003e\n\u003e git annex info\n\u003e [...]\n\u003e local annex keys: 0\n\u003e local annex size: 0 bytes\n\u003e annexed files in working tree: 0\n\u003e size of annexed files in working tree: 0 bytes\n\u003e\n\u003e The only solution to make this work with GitHub is removing those large\n\u003e git objects from the repo (throughout the entire history of the branch\n\u003e you're trying to push) and then track those large files with git-annex\n\u003e instead. You could rewrite the history to do this, but unless there's\n\u003e important information in the history, it'd be easiest to back up the\n\u003e current repo (just in case), wipe out the .git/ directory, and start fresh.\n\u003e Make sure those large files get added to the annex, not git.\n\u003e ------------------------------\n\u003e\n\u003e In terms of the original error reported, I don't think there's much to be\n\u003e done on DataLad's end, so I'll close this issue, but feel free to follow up\n\u003e with questions.\n\u003e\n\u003e —\n\u003e You are receiving this because you authored the thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3632?email_source=notifications\u0026email_token=AEGS2ZZDIHZNJ45U3AV2N63QIFJ6RA5CNFSM4ISQ2KZ2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOD6ALL7I#issuecomment-528528893\u003e,\n\u003e or mute the thread\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AEGS2Z3DKCQPRBP7XNZFOQLQIFJ6RANCNFSM4ISQ2KZQ\u003e\n\u003e .\n\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567721498,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODYxMDQ2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3632#issuecomment-528610466"},"message":"\u003e I had the suspect it was something like this when I saw annex size 0 bytes but I wonder, I thought github would accept ~50GiB\n\nI'm not clear on all the details of their size restrictions, but I do think it is much less than that.  [Here's a page][0] that mentions a 2GB push limit, which is consistent with what you're seeing.\n\n[0]: https://github.community/t5/Support-Protips/Working-with-large-files-and-repositories/ba-p/9343\n\n\u003e and I was sure that datalad commands would trigger git-annex automatically to add those files. \n\n`datalad add` and `datalad save` will typically add the files to annex, but here are some cases where they'll add files to git directly:\n\n  * They are called with the `--to-git` flag.\n\n  * git-annex is configured to store the content directly in git (more on that below).\n\n  * The repository isn't an annex repository.  This will happen if you call `datalad {add,save}` in a repository that was created with `git init` and `git annex init` has *not* been called.  If you're creating the repository with `datalad create`, you don't have to worry about this because by default it will create an annex repo (i.e, it will call `git annex init` for you).\n\n\u003e Maybe this can be implemented if the file content is higher than a certain threshold.\n\nContinuing from the second point above, git-annex [has a way][1] for configuring which files go where.  You can use this to implement the cutoff.  To use the example at that page, a `.gitattributes` file with\n\n```\n* annex.largefiles=(largerthan=100kb)\n```\n\nwould mean to put files larger than 100kb into annex.\n\nDataLad can configure .gitattributes one common case for you: track text files with git and put everything else into the annex.  You can run `datalad run-procedure cfg_text2git` in an existing annex repo (or use `datalad create -c text2git` when creating a new repo).  That will add the following line to the .gitattributes file:\n\n```\n* annex.largefiles=(not(mimetype=text/*))\n```\n\n[1]: https://git-annex.branchable.com/tips/largefiles/","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567721498,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI3NDE2Nzc4NQ=="},"target":"aaca0924c920c55048f028f1ae4a1e50983cc9cdb5bff55f8cbd4d2857f6a1c7","message":"\u003e I had the suspect it was something like this when I saw annex size 0 bytes but I wonder, I thought github would accept ~50GiB\n\nI'm not clear on all the details of their size restrictions, but I do think it is much less than that.  [Here's a page][0] that mentions a 2GB push limit, which is consistent with what you're seeing.\n\n[0]: https://github.community/t5/Support-Protips/Working-with-large-files-and-repositories/ba-p/9343\n\n\u003e and I was sure that datalad commands would trigger git-annex automatically to add those files. \n\n`datalad add` and `datalad save` will typically add the files to annex, but here are some cases where they'll add files to git directly:\n\n  * They are called with the `--to-git` flag.\n\n  * git-annex is configured to store the content directly in git (more on that below).\n\n 